@page
@model Portfolio.Pages.Skills.DatabaseModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Database";
}
<header class="page-header">
    <p class="page-kicker">
        <i class="bi bi-code-slash" aria-hidden="true"></i> Engineering &amp; Technology
    </p>
    <h1>
        @ViewData["Title"]
    </h1>
</header>
<div class="reading-layout">
    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="On this page">
        <h2>
            On this page
        </h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="#sql-server-and-relational-design">SQL Server and Relational Design</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#modern-ef-core-based-development">Modern EF Core Based Development</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#data-automation-and-local-services">Data Automation and Local Services</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#data-integration-and-practical-problem-solving">Data Integration and Practical Problem Solving</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="reading-main">
        <section class="content-panel prose">
            <h2 id="sql-server-and-relational-design">
                SQL Server and Relational Design
            </h2>
            <p>
                Database design and SQL Server work have been part of my career from early consulting projects through enterprise engineering.
                My background includes schema design, data validation, stored procedures, reporting support, database-driven applications,
                and data synchronization patterns between business systems.
            </p>
            <h2 id="modern-ef-core-based-development">
                Modern EF Core Based Development
            </h2>
            <p>
                Recent public repositories show my database work in a more modern application context. DotNetProjectStartup and Blazor-Chat-App
                both use SQL Server oriented application patterns, local development databases, Entity Framework Core, and solution structures
                that keep persistence concerns maintainable inside a larger application architecture.
            </p>
            <h2 id="data-automation-and-local-services">
                Data Automation and Local Services
            </h2>
            <p>
                My QA framework includes data automation and connection lifecycle support within a shared test host.
                Container-backed validation environments help isolate test resources, publish their endpoints,
                and retain cleanup ownership through test execution and diagnostics.
            </p>
            <p>
                The developer toolbox provides local SQL Server and PostgreSQL services, Redis caching,
                and Cosmos DB and DynamoDB emulators. My established database experience remains centered on SQL Server and relational data integration.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a asp-page="/Skills/Containers">Explore container-backed environments</a> and
                <a asp-page="/Skills/SystemsIntegration">systems integration and student-system experience</a>.
            </p>
            <h2 id="data-integration-and-practical-problem-solving">
                Data Integration and Practical Problem Solving
            </h2>
            <p>
                My experience also includes data migration and synchronization work, performance-minded query thinking, and the practical use
                of databases as part of broader systems. That includes work history items such as Encompass data sync services, reporting and
                warehousing support, and earlier custom data processing efforts.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="reading-aside">
        <section class="content-panel prose">
